# ==============================================================================
# HETEROGENEOUS HMS - ROOT ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION REFERENCE
# ==============================================================================
# Heterogeneous HMS uses decoupled environment files for its three subsystems:
#
# 1. Backend Service:     backend/.env.example      (Node.js/Express, MongoDB, Auth, SMS)
# 2. Frontend Web App:   frontend/.env.example     (React/Vite API endpoints)
# 3. OCR Microservice:   ocr-service/.env.example  (Python/FastAPI, Tesseract path, Secrets)
#
# To configure each subsystem:
#   Copy .env.example to .env in each corresponding directory:
#
#   PowerShell:
#     Copy-Item backend\.env.example backend\.env
#     Copy-Item frontend\.env.example frontend\.env
#     Copy-Item ocr-service\.env.example ocr-service\.env
#
# NEVER commit .env files containing real secrets, database URIs, or credentials!
# ==============================================================================
